From: iPlayPC
Subject: video: ask the host for HDR10

ihslib's protocol files predate Steam's HDR streaming. Add the newer fields we
need to the generated protobuf-c code (k_EStreamColorspace_HDR10,
CStreamingClientConfig.hdr_mode = 42 as an int32 carrying EStreamHDRMode, and
CStartVideoDataMsg.colorspace = 6), and an enableHdr session option that
advertises BT.709 plus HDR10 in the client caps, sets hdr_mode on and asks for
the Beautiful preset, which Steam needs before it sends HDR. Without it nothing
changes on the wire. The host's chosen colour space is passed to the
application as IHS_StreamVideoConfig.colorspace.

diff -ruN a/include/ihslib/session.h b/include/ihslib/session.h
--- a/include/ihslib/session.h
+++ b/include/ihslib/session.h
@@ -73,6 +73,12 @@
      */
     int32_t displayWidth;
     int32_t displayHeight;
+    /**
+     * Ask for HDR10 (needs enableHevc): advertises the HDR10 colour space, turns
+     * hdr_mode on and asks for the Beautiful quality preset, which Steam needs before
+     * it sends HDR. The host still decides; IHS_StreamVideoConfig.colorspace says what came.
+     */
+    bool enableHdr;
 } IHS_SessionConfig;
 
